  <content>
  <section><para>Students will complete the following questions to practice the skills they have learned in this lesson.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Which expression equals \(2^7\)?  </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(2+2+2+2+2+2+2\)</item>
      <item>\(2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)</item>
      <item>\(2 \cdot 7\)</item>
      <item>\(2+7\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> \(2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="2" type="enumerated">
  <item>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.</item>
  <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f84cb93fa8c368dc50ad53c8747843ba76f3d08f"/></media></figure></para>
  <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of years</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Amount in dollars</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>          
        <entry>
        0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          $2,000
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,150
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          2
        </entry>
        <entry>
          $2,300
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,450
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         4
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,600
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Investment A is a/n </item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> exponential function</para>
  <item>Investment B is a/n </item>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> linear function</para>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="3" type="enumerated">
  <item>The graph shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account A. The table shows the yearly balance, in dollars, of investment account B.</item>
  <para><figure><media alt="Graph of a function on grid."><image mime-type="image/png" src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/f84cb93fa8c368dc50ad53c8747843ba76f3d08f"/></media></figure></para>
  <table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
    <thead>
      <row>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Number of years</entry>
        <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">Amount in dollars</entry>
      </row>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <row>          
        <entry>
        0
        </entry>
        <entry>
          $2,000
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          1
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,150
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          2
        </entry>
        <entry>
          $2,300
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
          3
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,450
        </entry>
      </row>
      <row>
        <entry>
         4
        </entry>
        <entry>
         $2,600
        </entry>
      </row>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  
</list>
<para>Which of the following statements are true? <emphasis>Select two</emphasis> that apply.</para>
<list>
  <item aria-level="2"> Investment A has a higher initial balance than investment B. </item>
  <item aria-level="2"> Investment A has a common ratio. </item>
  <item aria-level="2"> Investment B has a common ratio. </item>
  <item aria-level="2"> Investment A is growing by the same number of dollars each year. </item>
  <item aria-level="2"> Investment B is growing by the same number of dollars each year. </item>
  <item aria-level="2"> After 12 years, investment B will result in more money. </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> Investment A has a common ratio &amp; After 12 years, investment B will result in more money.</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="4" type="enumerated">
  <item>Investment account 1 starts with a balance of $200 and doubles every year. Investment account 2 starts with $1,000 and increases by $100 each year. How many years does it take for each account to double?</item>
</list>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
  <item>Investment account 1 will double after</item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item> 1</item>
      <item>5</item>
      <item>10</item>
      <item>15</item>
    </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 1 year</para>
  <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated" start="2">
  <item>Investment account 2 will double after  </item>
  </list>
    <list>
      <item>1 </item>
      <item>5</item>
      <item>10 </item>
      <item>15 </item>
    </list>
  <para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> 10 years</para>

<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="5" type="enumerated">
  <item> A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. How many ants will there be 1 month later?   </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item> 10,003 </item>
      <item> 10,300 </item>
      <item> 30,000 </item>
      <item> 90,000 </item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>c. 30,000</para>
<para>6. A population of ants is 10,000 at the start of April. Since then, it triples each month. Which values complete the table? </para>
<table class="os-raise-skinnytable">
  <thead>
    <row>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">months since April</entry>
      <entry scope="col" class="emphasis">number of ants</entry>
    </row>
  </thead>
