      <entry>
      0
      </entry>
      <entry>
        10,000
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        1
      </entry>
      <entry>
      30,000
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        2
      </entry>
      <entry>
         
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
        3
      </entry>
      <entry>
         
      </entry>
    </row>
    <row>
      <entry>
       4
      </entry>
      <entry>
         
      </entry>
    </row>
  </tbody>
</table>

<list>
  <item> 50,000, 70,000, 90,000 </item>
  <item> 90,000, 270,000, 510,000 </item>
  <item> 40,000, 70,000, 110,000 </item>
  <item> 33,000, 33,300, 33,330 </item>
</list>
<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis> 90,000, 270,000, 510,000</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="7" type="enumerated">
  <item>A population of ants triples each month. If there are \(n\) ants in one month, which expression represents how many ants there will be one month later?  </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(
        3^n\) </item>
      <item>\(
        n^3\) </item>
      <item> \(3n\) </item>
      <item> \(n+3\) </item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(3n\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="8" type="enumerated">
  <item>A swimming pool contains 500 gallons of water. A hose is turned on, and it fills the pool at a rate of 24 gallons per minute. Which expression represents the amount of water in the pool, in gallons, after 8 minutes?  </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(500 \cdot 24 \cdot 8\)</item>
      <item>\(500+24+8\)</item>
      <item>\(500+24 \cdot 8\)</item>
      <item>\(500\cdot 248\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(500+24 \cdot 8\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="9" type="enumerated">
  <item>The population of a city is 100,000. It doubles each decade for 5 decades. <emphasis>Select the two</emphasis> expressions that represent the population of the city after 5 decades.   </item>
</list>
    <list>
      <item>\(32,000\)</item>
      <item>\(320,000\)</item>
      <item>\(100,000 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)</item>
      <item>\(100,000 \cdot 5^2\)</item>
      <item>\(100,000 \cdot 2^5\)</item>
    </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer:</emphasis> \(100,000 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\) &amp; \(100,000 \cdot 2^5\)</para>
<list class="os-raise-noindent" start="10" type="enumerated">
  <item>Bank account C starts with $10 and doubles each week. Bank account D starts with $1,000 and grows by $500 each week.</item>
</list>
<para>When will account C contain more money than account D? </para>
  <list>
    <item> Account C will contain more money than account D after 2 weeks.</item>
    <item> Account C will never contain more money than account D.  </item>
    <item> Account C will contain more money than account D after 7 weeks.</item>
    <item> Account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks.</item>
  </list>

<para><emphasis>Answer: </emphasis>Account C will contain more money than account D after 10 weeks.</para></list></section>
